{"authored" [{"question" "q-1052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-5=3y \\\\ 6+y=4x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035972/state.json" "file_sha256" "2de3fc6a48919c3815ae63440e108e5108ed3db5e61050b64a8a98b9ec9ad3b7" "basis" 1304 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035972/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-1052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $x,y$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ -4x+y=-6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix  is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035972/state.json" "file_sha256" "2de3fc6a48919c3815ae63440e108e5108ed3db5e61050b64a8a98b9ec9ad3b7" "basis" 1304 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035972/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-1052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035972/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "58a528cff20e81240a296